section.p:
        In the view: 


Create the STable.

STable rosterTable = new STable(); 



Set the STable selector string to the name of the arraylist in the model: 

rosterTable.setSelector("rosterEntries"); 



Set the column selector strings to show which fields in the ItemModel to display in the STable: 

String[] columnSelects = {"name","position","number"}; 
rosterTable.setColumnSelectors(columnSelects); 



Set the column names: 

String[] columnNames = {"Name","Position","Number"};//set the column names/column header values 
rosterTable.setColumnNames(columnNames); 



        If any of the column selectors map to boolean getter methods, the Scope framework will automatically render 
        that column as a checkbox. You may also create a specific cell editor or renderer for an STable, just as with a JTable.

subsection.p:
          Setting editable columns using the STableModel: 


Define in a boolean array if columns are to be editable.

boolean[] b = {true, false, false, false, true};



Extract the STableModel from the STable and call the setEditableColumns method. 


STableModel tableModel = (STableModel)examTable.getModel(); 
tableModel.setEditableColumns(b);
